cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fiducio in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Fiducio: Model-agnostic post-hoc calibration for 2D and 3D semantic segmentation"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-24"
authors:
  - name: "Fiducio maintainers (fiducio-ai)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fiducio-ai/Fiducio"
url: "https://fiducio-ai.github.io/Fiducio/"
license: "Apache-2.0"
type: software
keywords:
  - calibration
  - semantic segmentation
  - uncertainty
  - pytorch
abstract: >
  Fiducio is a model-agnostic Python library for post-hoc calibration of 2D and
  3D semantic segmentation models. It provides a consistent fit / transform API
  for temperature, vector, matrix, Dirichlet and class-conditional matrix scaling
  calibrators that operate on logits or probabilities produced by any segmentation
  model.
